#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0276 expect=noViolation domain=TS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when a record exists with TSPARMCD equal to 'STYPE' and TSVAL equal to 'INTERVENTIONAL', but TSVAL is empty for the record where TSPARMCD equals 'TRT'.
#note "Cross-half exclusivity: TRT has no record at all. That is CDISC-CG0276-A's case, not this rule's -- the record half must stay silent so the split neither duplicates nor hides a finding."
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S01 | TS | 1 | STYPE | INTERVENTIONAL
S01 | TS | 2 | TITLE | A Study of Drug X
---
